From 7c94f333585df083a01bfe2eb1d1aea6bd7203c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 09:06:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: stm32: use dev_dbg() for missing OPP-v2 message

Missing OPP-v2 support is not necessarily an error. The driver already
returns -ENODEV when no OPP node is found, which can be part of the
expected probe flow.

Replace dev_err() with dev_dbg() to avoid reporting this normal case as
an error while keeping the message available for debugging.

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Idbe1b043a909deda8fbd4e0247a4bd7aa8242356
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/579506
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/stm32-cpufreq.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/stm32-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/stm32-cpufreq.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ static int stm32_cpufreq_probe(struct pl
 	}
 	opp_node = dev_pm_opp_of_get_opp_desc_node(cpu_dev);
 	if (!opp_node) {
-		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "OPP-v2 not supported\n");
+		dev_dbg(&pdev->dev, "OPP-v2 not supported\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
